  ('sta-132-statistical-computing', 'STA 132: Statistical Computing', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, Faculty of Engineering, Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Statistics', '100 Level', 'Yearly sales for 2003 to 2007 are 70, 74, 80, 86 and 90. With the middle year (2005) coded 0, the least-squares trend line is:', '["y = 70 + 5.2x","y = 80 + 5.2x","y = 80 + 7.2x","y = 60 + 5.26x"]'::jsonb, 1, 'With coded $x$ summing to zero, $a = \bar{y} = 80$ and $b = \sum xy/\sum x^{2} = 52/10 = 5.2$.', 'Trend Analysis', false, 'second', 2),
  ('sta-132-statistical-computing', 'STA 132: Statistical Computing', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, Faculty of Engineering, Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Statistics', '100 Level', 'Using that trend line, the estimated sales for 2010 (coded $x = 5$) are:', '["96","110","106","100"]'::jsonb, 2, '$y = 80 + 5.2(5) = 106$.', 'Trend Analysis', false, 'second', 2),
  ('sta-132-statistical-computing', 'STA 132: Statistical Computing', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, Faculty of Engineering, Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Statistics', '100 Level', 'A Type I error is committed when:', '["the null hypothesis is rightly rejected","the null hypothesis is accepted","the sample is not random","the null hypothesis is wrongly rejected"]'::jsonb, 3, 'Rejecting a true $H_0$ is a Type I error.', 'Types of Error', false, 'second', 2),
  ('sta-132-statistical-computing', 'STA 132: Statistical Computing', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, Faculty of Engineering, Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Statistics', '100 Level', 'The distribution X: 12, 20, 27, 33, Z, 54 has frequencies 8, 16, 48, 90, 30, 8 and mean 31.87. The missing value $Z$ is:', '["42","36.6","46.1","38.4"]'::jsonb, 0, '$\sum f = 200$, so $\sum fx = 6374$. The known terms sum to 5114, so $30Z = 1260$ and $Z = 42$.', 'Missing Frequency Problems', false, 'second', 2),
  ('sta-132-statistical-computing', 'STA 132: Statistical Computing', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Social Sciences, Faculty of Engineering, Faculty of Biological Sciences', 'Statistics', '100 Level', 'The "best-fit" line drawn on a scatter diagram is intended to:', '["join every data point","minimise the overall deviation of the points from the line","always pass through the origin","maximise the slope"]'::jsonb, 1, 'The line summarises the trend in the data.', 'Simple Linear Regression', false, 'second', 2),
